+      "prompt": "Create one square 1024x1024 image, a fresh original painting generated entirely from text, with no reference images. Style priority: an authentic Leonora Carrington surrealist painting, fully painted from its first mark, never a photograph with a filter. An immense, prominent woman in her early 30s with curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses and a mustard-yellow knit sweater enjoys coffee in a moonlit alchemical kitchen, surrounded by dream animals. Show her as an elongated, monumental seated nearly full-length figure towering among small dream animals and intricate folklore details. Let surrealist anatomy, impossible spatial relationships and a tilted kitchen floor dictate the composition. Coffee and the nearby croissant are magical ritual objects; steam unfurls into strange delicate forms. Muted mineral greens and bone dominate, with aged ochre mustard and rust auburn accents. Finely layered painted surfaces, intricate otherworldly creatures, still nocturnal atmosphere. The woman is the large dominant subject, not a tiny figure in a room. No text, captions, letters, calligraphy, signatures, logos, borders or watermarks."
+    },
+    {
+      "file": "./styles/626-chuck-close.png",
+      "prompt": "Create one square 1024x1024 image, a fresh original painting generated entirely from text, with no reference images. Style priority: an authentic Chuck Close painted grid portrait. An extreme frontal face crop fills almost the whole canvas: a woman in her early 30s with curly auburn shoulder-length hair, visible freckles and round tortoiseshell glasses. Her expression conveys quiet pleasure in her coffee. A thin band of mustard-yellow knit sweater remains along the bottom; a coffee cup enters the lower corner with a small nearby croissant partially cropped by the canvas. Construct EVERY part of the image from an unmistakably visible regular grid of individually handmade painted marks: each cell contains irregular nested colored ovals, rings, lozenges and dabs; abstract colored cells coalesce into a readable face from a distance. Glasses and freckles remain readable through the painted cells. Rich chromatic optical mixtures and tactile paint. Large grid cells visible at normal viewing size. The grid and handmade cell language are the substance of the painting, not a pixelation effect or filter laid over a photo. Face monumental, direct, close, cropped; no cafe scene. No text, captions, letters, signatures, logos, borders or watermarks."
+    },
+    {
+      "file": "./styles/627-nihonga.png",
+      "prompt": "Generate one fresh square 1024x1024 image ENTIRELY FROM TEXT, with no reference images. An authentic Nihonga painting on silk in soft mineral pigments and a restrained touch of gold. A woman in her early 30s with curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses and a mustard-yellow knit sweater is large and prominent, seated in a quiet interior enjoying a ceramic cup of coffee with a croissant on a nearby dish. Depict her in a large graceful seated profile, her softly stylized facial features and curved silhouette rendered with delicate pigment layers on luminous silk. Asymmetrical Japanese painted space, subtly flattened forms, understated facial modeling; delicate seasonal flowering branches, quiet indoor light, softly granular mineral color. This is a handmade Nihonga painting, not a woodblock print, not an ink sketch and not a photo with a filter. Absolutely NO WRITING anywhere: no calligraphy, no glyphs, no artist signature, no hanko, no chop, no red stamp, no seal, no monogram, no inscriptions, no captions, no logos, no watermark. Leave the lower corners entirely free of any signature-like symbols; only natural painted surfaces and pigments there. No decorative border. The round glasses, freckles, curly auburn hair and mustard knitted sweater should remain clearly recognizable within the painted style."
+    },
+    {
+      "file": "./styles/628-edmund-dulac.png",
+      "prompt": "Create one square 1024x1024 image, a fresh original watercolor generated entirely from text, with no reference images. Style priority: an authentic Edmund Dulac fairy-tale watercolor, with powdery soft washes and hazy jewel colors in a moonlit garden. A large half-length woman in her early 30s with curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses and a mustard-yellow knit sweater enjoys fragrant coffee, cradling the cup close to her lips while turning in a gentle three-quarter pose. A nearby croissant rests on a little garden ledge. The half-length figure fills most of the image with an elegant fairy-tale silhouette; use delicately stylized anatomy and a dreamlike off-center composition. Moonlit flowers and foliage, misty indigo and turquoise shadows, muted amethyst and ochre, subtle luminous highlights. Powdery watercolor blooms, translucent layered washes and gently dissolving edges, enchanting early twentieth-century storybook painting with depth and atmosphere. Not a flat miniature, not a pen-and-ink drawing, not a photograph or filter. Her freckles, round glasses, auburn curls and mustard knit remain recognizable within the watercolor idiom. No text, captions, letters, signatures, logos, decorative frame or watermarks."
+    }
+  ]
